  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Crazy Eights. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Crazy Eights is a popular shedding card game, especially beloved by children. The objective is simple: be the first player to discard all your cards. Players take turns playing cards to a central discard pile, matching either the rank or suit of the top card. The eponymous "crazy" 8s are wild cards that can be played on anything and allow the player to change the suit.',
    objective: 'Avoid being the player left with all the cards, the Hund or dog.',
    gameplay: 'Deal all cards to four players. The player with the two of clubs begins. Players must beat the previous card where possible or pick up cards from the table; individual trump suits create different winning relations for each player. When a player has to take the pile, the next player starts a fresh pile.',
    keyRules: [
      'There is no positive winner; the game identifies the loser.',
      'Each player has an individual trump suit.',
      'Picking up the pile changes the next lead and the number of cards in play.',
    ],
